gpu-bridge: rebuild GL objects at the surface-update chokepoint

Continuing a saved Xbox project under the GL renderer aborted on a settled
frame: a 2D title or menu resumes by replaying clear_surface / image_blit,
which call pgraph_gl_surface_update straight from the pgraph command stream -
not through draw_begin, get_framebuffer_surface or sync, the doors patch 0011
guards. After a cross-session load the framebuffer and surface textures name
a host GL context that is gone, so update_surface_part binds a gone framebuffer,
it is never GL_FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE, and its assert aborts (SIGABRT surfaces as
miniBox unimplemented syscall 200). Every path to that assert funnels through
pgraph_gl_surface_update, so check the context there, at the one shared door,
and rebuild before a gone name is bound. Cheap and a no-op once the objects
match this session, so same-session loads and determinism are untouched.

diff --git a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/surface.c b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/surface.c
--- a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/surface.c
+++ b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/surface.c
@@ -1335,6 +1335,18 @@
 void pgraph_gl_surface_update(NV2AState *d, bool upload, bool color_write,
                            bool zeta_write)
 {
+    /* Every path that binds a surface to the framebuffer funnels through here
+     * (update_surface_part below), and after a cross-session savestate load the
+     * framebuffer and surface textures name a context that is gone. A 2D title
+     * or menu reaches this by clear_surface or image_blit - not by draw_begin,
+     * get_framebuffer_surface or sync, the doors already guarded - so the gone
+     * framebuffer gets bound, is never GL_FRAMEBUFFER_COMPLETE, and the assert
+     * in update_surface_part aborts (SIGABRT -> miniBox syscall 200). Rebuild
+     * the context here, at the one door they all share, before that happens.
+     * A no-op once the objects match this session, so same-session loads and
+     * determinism are untouched. */
+    pgraph_gl_check_context(d);
+
     PGRAPHState *pg = &d->pgraph;
     PGRAPHGLState *r = pg->gl_renderer_state;
 
